  "research_notes": "Current supported within-data associations: feature_027=1 stronger dependency (validated main about +0.79 to +0.84; stable in feature_040 high +0.878 and low +0.730; feature_053==10 +0.744; feature_051 strata and rare marker contexts large but sometimes imprecise). feature_037=1 stronger dependency (validated main about +0.80; feature_053==10 +0.793; accepted across several contexts). feature_002=1 weaker dependency (validated main about +0.78 to +0.83; feature_040 high +0.908 and low +0.756; feature_051 high +0.840). feature_010=1 weaker dependency (validated about +0.42 to +0.47; feature_051 high +0.426; inside rare feature_027=1 underpowered). feature_063=1 stronger dependency (validated main about +0.23 to +0.25; high feature_051 accepted after validation about +0.20 to +0.26; feature_040 high accepted +0.306 with CI lower above threshold). feature_063 in feature_040 low is not accepted (+0.143, lower near zero). feature_063 in feature_053==10 is unresolved/deferred (+0.201, CI 0.088 to 0.315). feature_063 in low feature_051 (H157, +0.249, CI 0.114 to 0.385) is unresolved active and validation requested to test stability across feature_051. feature_003 remains borderline/uncertain. feature_007, feature_058, feature_015, feature_017, and most tested interactions are rejected or underpowered. Nominal feature_059, feature_052, and feature_054 contrasts assessed so far are null. Proposed next feature_063 interaction with feature_040 is only a formal test of the high versus low direct subgroup contrast and should be interpreted cautiously because it is one of many tested contrasts. All conclusions remain observational within the supplied dataset and do not establish causality, mechanism, coding interpretation, or generalizability.",
