  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For the direction -1 feature_037, feature_027, and feature_063 claims, a positive signed estimate means the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast was negative, i.e. the exposed group had a more negative composite dependency score and therefore stronger dependency. For the direction +1 feature_002 and feature_010 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group had less negative outcome values and therefore weaker dependency. H171 and H172 test feature_037 in the two median feature_040 strata. The estimates are +0.838 (95% CI 0.746 to 0.930) in feature_040 >= -7.353 and +0.825 (95% CI 0.730 to 0.920) in feature_040 <= -7.353. Both are far above the 0.15-unit threshold, both have lower bounds well above the threshold, and both are consistent with the previously validated feature_037 main and subgroup results. I accept and close H171 and H172 as within-data associations; they show that the feature_037 association is not confined to the feature_040 median strata used so far. H173 and H174 test feature_010 in the same feature_040 strata. The signed estimates are +0.405 (95% CI 0.256 to 0.555) and +0.435 (95% CI 0.309 to 0.562). Both lower bounds exceed the threshold and the directions are consistent with the accepted feature_010 weaker-dependency main association. I accept and close both. H177 completes the feature_051 stratum pair for feature_037: in feature_051 <= 2.6735 the estimate is +0.779 (95% CI 0.686 to 0.872), far above threshold and consistent with the accepted high feature_051 result. I accept and close H177. H178 and H179 complete feature_051 <= median for feature_002 and feature_010. feature_002 gives +0.822 (95% CI 0.736 to 0.907) and feature_010 gives +0.418 (95% CI 0.291 to 0.545). Both are threshold-sized and consistent with their accepted high feature_051 and main associations. I accept and close both. H180 through H183 extend the extreme feature_053 == 1