  "narrative": "No assessments are due and independent validation budget is exhausted, so I register discovery-only comparisons designed to localize two remaining areas of uncertainty: whether feature_003 can be supported outside highly selected core-negative contexts, and whether the smaller feature_063 association is stable, attenuated, or context-dependent in clean contexts with feature_027=0. The first two claims test feature_003 under direction -1, where a positive signed estimate means raw exposed-minus-comparator outcome_001 is more negative, i.e. stronger composite dependency. H215 showed a conditional feature_003 effect only in a very selected other-core-zero plus feature_063=0 plus feature_027=0 context, so the first new proposal broadens that to other-core-zero while allowing feature_063 and feature_027 to vary. The second broadens the overall feature_003 contrast by excluding the rare feature_027=1 group, testing whether the near-threshold overall signal is diluted by rare feature_027. Both remain hypothesis tests for whether feature_003 is a general or merely highly context-specific predictor. The next four proposals test feature_063 under direction -1 within low feature_040, high feature_030, high feature_053, and low feature_053, each additionally requiring feature_002=0, feature_037=0, feature_010=0, and feature_027=0. This clean core-negative context was previously informative and threshold precise for feature_063; applying it to strata where marginal feature_063 effects were weaker or imprecise checks whether those weak effects are attributable to co-occurrence with other strong markers or represent genuine attenuation by the numeric stratum. If any of these lower bounds exceed 0.15 composite dependency-score units, that supports a precise context-specific stronger-dependency effect for feature_063. If point estimates remain near threshold with lower bounds far below, feature_063 should remain described as directionally consistent but context-dependent. The two f053 interaction proposals test whether feature_002 and feature_010 effects are attenuated in one feature_053 stratum. Because raw feature_002 and feature_010 main contrasts are positive for direction +1, representing weaker dependency in exposed groups, an attenuating interaction inside the named subgroup has a negative raw subgroup-minus-complement interaction; I therefore set claim direction -1 and anticipated raw direction -1 so a positive returned signed estimate supports attenuation. The final proposal tests feature_063 effect modification by high feature_040 within the core-negative eligible population; raw feature_063 contrasts are negative, so if high feature_040 shows a more negative feature_063 contrast than low feature_040, the raw high-minus-low interaction is negative, consistent with direction -1. All comparisons are subject to the 20-observation per cell rule and will be judged by signed point estimates, 95% Welch intervals, and the 0.15-unit threshold. These are dataset-only associations, not causal, biological, coding-level, single-gene-knockout, or generalizability claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 17 explore plan. Validation budget exhausted; continue discovery only. Retained accepted core dataset conclusions: feature_027=1 and feature_037=1 mark stronger composite dependency under direction -1; feature_002=1 and feature_010=1 mark weaker dependency under direction +1; feature_063=1 is smaller, directionally consistent, context-dependent stronger-dependency signal; feature_003=1 is supported only in highly selected contexts and near threshold. Active registered claims H76-H82, H175, H216 remain useful; no duplicates registered for those. New proposals: (1) feature_003 in other-core-zero but not requiring feature_063=0 or feature_027=0, to see whether conditional feature_003 effect broadens; parent H215. (2) feature_003 overall excluding feature_027=1, to test rare-marker dilution; parent H26. (3-6) feature_063 in low feature_040, high feature_030, high feature_053, and low feature_053, each in feature_002=0, feature_037=0, feature_010=0, feature_027=0 context; parents H162, H203, H160, H191. These check whether weak/imprecise feature_063 stratum effects are confounded by other core markers or represent true context attenuation. (7) feature_002 interaction high feature_053, direction -1, parent H218, testing whether high feature_053 attenuates the positive raw feature_002 weaker-dependency contrast suggested by low-feature_053 interaction. (8) feature_010 interaction low feature_053, direction -1, parent H219, testing complementary localization. (9) feature_063 interaction high feature_040 within core-negative eligibility, direction -1, parent H170, formal clean-context check of feature_040 modification. Interpretation rules: for direction -1 mean differences, positive signed = raw more negative outcome = stronger dependency; for direction +1, positive signed = raw less negative outcome = weaker dependency. For interaction claims with direction -1 in P7-P9, positive signed supports raw attenuation or stronger high-feature_040 feature_063 effect as registered. Accept only if point and interval justify exceeding 0.15 units; lower bounds near or below threshold require context-dependent language. No causal or generalizability claims."
