  "narrative": "All twelve due Welch comparisons are valid under the minimum-cell rule and are interpreted using the signed estimates for the registered directions. For direction +1 claims, positive signed estimates mean the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is positive, i.e. outcome_001 is less negative and composite dependency is weaker. For direction -1 claims, positive signed estimates mean the raw contrast is negative, i.e. outcome_001 is more negative and composite dependency is stronger. The central new evidence supports marker-specific core-context associations. H76 and H82 give signed feature_002 contrasts of +0.784 and +0.811 with lower bounds well above 0.15, supporting weaker composite dependency for feature_002=1 when feature_037/feature_010 or feature_063/feature_010 are reference. H77 and H78 support the same feature_002 direction in feature_037-present/feature_010-absent and feature_037-absent/feature_010-present contexts (+0.722 lower +0.628; +0.937 lower +0.748). H79 supports feature_037=1 as stronger composite dependency when feature_002=0 and feature_010=0: +0.814, lower +0.768. H80 supports feature_010=1 as weaker composite dependency when feature_002=0 and feature_037=0: +0.402, lower +0.302. These accepted claims close the main concern that the large feature_002, feature_037, and feature_010 associations are driven only by the rare feature_027=1 group or only by the full population. H81 supports feature_063=1 as a smaller stronger-dependency marker in a clean context with feature_002=0 and feature_037=0: +0.240, interval +0.141 to +0.339. The interval excludes zero, but the lower bound is slightly below 0.15, so this should be described as directionally supported but not threshold-precise. H175 tests feature_063 effect modification by high feature_051. The signed interaction is -0.046, interval -0.238 to +0.146, opposite to the claimed direction and compatible with zero; I reject and close it. H221 and H222 localize feature_003. H221 tests other-core-zero without requiring feature_063=0 or feature_027=0: signed +0.144, lower +0.083, upper +0.204. The interval supports the direction but the point estimate is below the 0.15-unit threshold, so I reject this as evidence of a threshold-meaningful association. H222 excludes the rare feature_027=1 group: +0.158, lower +0.078, upper +0.238. This is directionally consistent and the point estimate slightly exceeds threshold, but the lower bound is far below threshold; I accept it only as a conditional feature_003 association within feature_027=0, not as evidence of a general predictor and not as threshold-precise. H223 and H224 test feature_063 in low feature_040 and high feature_030 clean core-negative contexts. H223 gives +0.193, lower +0.082, and H224 gives +0.223, lower +0.053. Both intervals exclude zero, so they support the registered direction, but their lower bounds do not establish threshold precision and the high feature_030 context is especially uncertain because of small exposed cells and multiplicity among feature_063 strata. I accept them as context-dependent directional evidence, not as uniformly precise feature_063 main effects. Critical audit: all context exclusions were pre-specified as observational context checks, not outcome-selected groups; all cells met the 20-observation rule. The robust lower bounds for feature_002, feature_037, and feature_010 make chance alone an implausible sole explanation. The smaller feature_063 and conditional feature_003 results require interval-aware language and remain dataset-only associations. No causal, biological, coding-level, single-gene-knockout, or external generalizability claim is supported. Validation is not requested because the independent validation budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 17 appraise. Validation budget exhausted; no validate request. Closed due comparisons. Core-context acceptances: H76-H78 and H82 support feature_002=1 as weaker composite dependency in selected contexts; H79 supports feature_037=1 as stronger dependency with feature_002/feature_010 reference; H80 supports feature_010=1 as weaker dependency with feature_002/feature_037 reference; these lower bounds are well above 0.15. H81 supports feature_063=1 as smaller stronger-dependency marker in feature_002=0/feature_037=0 context, but lower bound 0.141 is below threshold, so not threshold precise. H175 rejected: feature_063 by high feature_051 interaction is wrong direction/compatible with zero. H221 rejected: feature_003 in other-core-zero without feature_063/feature_027 restrictions has point 0.144 below threshold. H222 accepted as conditional feature_003=1 stronger dependency among feature_027=0, point 0.158 but lower 0.078, not threshold precise. H223/H224 accepted as directional feature_063 context evidence in low feature_040 and high feature_030 clean core-negative contexts, but lower bounds 0.082 and 0.053 mean not threshold precise; high feature_030 remains especially uncertain. Overall retained conclusions: robust dataset-only associations are feature_027=1 stronger, feature_037=1 stronger, feature_002=1 weaker, feature_010=1 weaker; feature_063=1 is smaller and context-dependent; feature_003=1 remains conditional and near threshold. Remaining active claims include H216, H225-H229, H36, H41, H165-H167, and other deferred contexts. Future work should avoid treating feature_063 or feature_003 as general main effects unless lower bounds exceed 0.15 or additional discovery evidence strengthens them."
