  "narrative": "No new validation arrived and no validation budget remains, so this synthesis is a dataset-only final report using the stated 0.15 composite dependency-score threshold rule. The robust threshold-supported associations are: feature_027=1 is associated with stronger composite dependency, H128 discovery +0.792 [0.676,0.907] and validation +0.836 [0.672,1.001]; feature_037=1 is associated with stronger composite dependency, H24 discovery +0.833 [0.767,0.898] and validation +0.795 [0.695,0.896]; feature_002=1 is associated with weaker dependency in the claimed direction, H63 discovery +0.832 [0.766,0.897] and validation +0.783 [0.688,0.878]; and feature_010=1 is associated with weaker dependency, H37 discovery +0.423 [0.327,0.520] and validation +0.471 [0.334,0.607]. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is negative, so exposed has more negative outcome_001 and stronger dependency; for direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means exposed has weaker dependency. All four main findings have lower bounds far above threshold and are accepted in many subgroup contrasts, but most direct interaction tests involving these variables were null, so the subgroup acceptances indicate persistence of the main associations rather than proof of effect modification. The main unresolved predictor is feature_063. Its overall effect is not threshold-precise because H27 is validated at +0.248 [0.109,0.388], with the lower bound below threshold, so the overall main effect remains unresolved. However, feature_063 has threshold-supported mean-difference contrasts in selected contexts, especially the clean core-negative population feature_002=0, feature_037=0, feature_010=0, feature_027=0, where H213 is +0.260 [0.182,0.338], and in high numeric contexts including high feature_053, H225 +0.295 [0.194,0.395], high feature_040, H233 +0.321 [0.210,0.431], high feature_051, H234 +0.311 [0.197,0.426], and high-high combinations such as H236, H237, and H245. These accepted feature_063 contexts are numerous and overlapping, so they should be described as context-dependent, post-hoc selected associations rather than a uniform main effect. The interaction tests do not establish a threshold-supported modifier: H247 is +0.086 [-0.076,0.248], H249 is +0.104 [-0.053,0.260], H250 is +0.168 [-0.056,0.393], H252 is +0.121 [-0.078,0.320], and even the most suggestive H251 is +0.268 [0.047,0.489] with a lower bound far below threshold. The most informative next analysis is therefore a single pre-specified high-high context interaction in the core-negative population, combining high feature_053 and high feature_040. This registered proposal asks whether the accepted high-context feature_063 contrasts represent genuine effect modification or selected additive contexts. Feature_003 remains weak and below threshold: H93 is +0.142 [0.064,0.221], H95 validated is +0.151 [0.056,0.246], and H253 is +0.115 [0.045,0.185]; it is not a threshold predictor and its interactions are unsupported. Negative findings include no threshold main effects for the constructed binary markers feature_007, feature_058, or feature_015 and no supported interactions with feature_038, feature_018, or feature_036; feature_017 is null after validation; feature_047 is null and numerically redundant with feature_021; feature_031 and most other binary features are subthreshold or null; feature_060 is null; and feature_024, feature_046, feature_052, feature_054, feature_059, and feature_061 categorical contrasts do not support threshold associations. Key negative interaction findings include rejected feature_002 by feature_010 after validation, rejected feature_063 by feature_040 or feature_051 interactions in several contexts, and rejected feature_003 interaction claims. These conclusions are associations in this dataset only and do not establish causality, biological mechanism, coding-level meaning, single-gene knockout interpretation, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 20 synthesis final report. No validation requests remain; all current assessments are discovery-only except previously validated claims, and the threshold rule remains signed lower bound >0.15 composite dependency-score units. Robust accepted dataset-only associations: feature_027=1 stronger dependency (H128 validated +0.836 [0.672,1.001]); feature_037=1 stronger dependency (H24 validated +0.795 [0.695,0.896]); feature_002=1 weaker dependency (H63 validated +0.783 [0.688,0.878]); feature_010=1 weaker dependency (H37 validated +0.471 [0.334,0.607]). These are large relative to threshold and persistent across contexts, but accepted subgroup contrasts should not be read as interactions because most direct interaction tests are null. feature_063 is context-dependent: overall H27 unresolved (validated lower 0.109), but accepted mean-difference contexts include H213 core-negative, H225 high feature_053, H233 high feature_040, H234 high feature_051, H236 and H237 high-high combinations, H245 high feature_053 and high feature_040, H214 low feature_030, and H161 high feature_040. No feature_063 interaction reached threshold: H247, H249, H250, H251, H252, and H248 all have lower bounds below 0.15 or cross zero. feature_003 remains subthreshold and contextually weak: H93, H95, H253 have lower bounds below threshold; H254 interaction is opposite direction and rejected. Negative/null: feature_007, feature_058, feature_015, feature_017, feature_047, feature_031, feature_060, feature_024, feature_046, feature_052, feature_054, feature_059, feature_061, and most interactions including feature_002 by feature_010, feature_063 by feature_040 or feature_051, feature_003 by feature_053, feature_002 or feature_010 by feature_053, and feature_027 or feature_037 context interactions. Next registered analysis: one parsimonious feature_063 interaction in core-negative eligibility using high feature_053 and high feature_040, linked to accepted H245; acceptance requires signed lower bound >0.15, otherwise feature_063 remains a selected-context marker without proven effect modification. No causal, biological, coding-level, single-gene-knockout, or generalizability claims are supported."
