ncy. For interactions, anticipated_direction -1 means I expect the raw interaction to be negative because the feature_063 stronger-dependency contrast is expected to be more negative in the high subgroup than in the complement. I will accept only if the signed 95% Welch lower bound exceeds 0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction. Third-quartile mean differences with lower bounds above threshold would support a context dose-response; third-quartile interactions with lower bounds above threshold would support genuine effect modification. If mean differences remain threshold-supported but interactions remain null or subthreshold, the safer interpretation remains context-dependent selected associations rather than modification. I also close null-inclusive median interaction claims H247, H249, H250, and H252 because their intervals include zero and are far below the 0.15 threshold; H251 remains unresolved but closed because it is positive and excludes zero yet does not meet the threshold rule. All conclusions are dataset-only associations and do not establish causality, biological mechanism, coding-level meaning, single-gene-knockout interpretation, or external generalizability.",
